# Rendered video and audio never belong in version control. Eight sample
# MP4s once sat in auto_editor/sample_output and made this repository 169 MB,
# 166 MB of which was those files. update.bat downloads the branch as a zip,
# so every single update pulled all of them again — the reason updating took
# hours instead of seconds. They are still in the history if one is needed:
#
#   git show HEAD~1:auto_editor/sample_output/pro_demo.mp4 > pro_demo.mp4
#
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.avi
*.webm
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a

# Built by the tool, per machine
library.db
library.db-wal
library.db-shm
settings.txt

# The picture model, and the vectors it produces. Both are large, both are
# reproducible from the footage on the machine that holds it, and neither
# means anything on another machine — the weights are a 1 GB download and the
# vectors are ~4 MB per episode. Tracking either would put this repository
# straight back into the state that made update.bat take hours.
models/
*_visual/
proof/
built/
out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
